Interactive edits of a mesh light whose light filter comes from its node graph (primvars:arnold:light:shaders)

see #2799

A grey wall is only lit by a mesh light, whose node graph has a light_decay filter cutting the light before it reaches
the wall. The intensity of the mesh light is edited, the filter must be kept even though the light shaders primvar
isn't synced. The light shaders are then removed and set back, the filter being removed and added again.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive render session,
and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image. The legacy reader keeps the filter when the light shaders are removed, this is
reported as a known issue.

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
